title The wall was a glob and the law is a graph
prompt Autonomous lap -- Incense, law lane; take the next agent-doable work Lindy-first, crux-first.
rota lap 4481, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; the row reads by pressing each boundary to see whether the hand passes through, so the lap walked the fence line of the law rooms rather than opening new work.
think Pressed the first fence: every witness the .claude/rules pages name as their enforcement, checked against disk and against construction/standing-equipment.kyri. All 30 exist and all 30 are rostered -- 24 tier lap, 6 tier cadence. That post stands.
think My first parse of the roster answered UNFOUND for reds_citation, which is rostered at tier lap. The awk flushed a record on a blank line, and a record followed immediately by comment lines never flushed. Rebuilt the parse to flush on the next guard header; it then read 290 of 290 records and the finding held.
think Pressed the second fence, which is ascii-first.md's own named open question: the ENFORCE roster is two directory globs while the law is a graph, so a page a rule tells a reader to read FIRST was walled by nothing. A hand swept five such pages to zero on 20260908 and left the roster unchanged.
think Measured what actually held those five pages afterward: seven characters of ratchet slack. One em dash in context/RADIANT_STYLE.md reddened nothing; eight of them reddened a total naming no page.
think Derived the enforced set from the rule rooms' own citations -- Markdown links and backticked paths both, since the law writes canon both ways -- filtered to living tracked pages, reading past dated testimony, closed stacks, vendored sources, fixtures, and citations this tree does not carry. 33 pages.
think A hand grep said all 33 already stood at zero, which would have made the widening free. The widened scan refused two of them. The grep had spelled its octal class inside single quotes, where [\300-\377] is a set of digits and a backslash rather than the high-byte range, so it answered a clean zero for everything it read -- this meter's own subject turned back on the hand measuring it, the second loose instrument in one lap.
obs Derived rather than typed, for the reason the globs are globs: a page the law begins citing tomorrow is walled the day it lands. The one thing derivation can do that a glob cannot is drop a page silently by an edit made elsewhere, so enforce_globbed and enforce_derived print separately and a drop is legible in the census.
obs The ceiling keeps the seven of slack it already stood on and takes none of the ninety-nine, so this lap is credited with nothing it did not repair.
obs The Cursor twin .cursor/rules/ascii-first.mdc already carries different text for this passage, so it is one of the 38 two-way drifted pairs custody gate %194 holds. Left untouched.
file tools/fixtures/a/ascii_document_scan.sh the derivation, the widened ENFORCE loop, the ratchet exclusion so a page is priced once, and the ceiling arc 3331 -> 3232
file tools/fixtures/a/ascii_document_control.sh nineteen legs for the derived canon, each shown from both sides; 44 -> 63 checks, 0 fails
file tools/a/ascii_document_witness.rish the claim line names the canon and its own check count
file .claude/rules/ascii-first.md the law records the answer to the question it named, with what the five hand-swept pages had holding them
file session-logs/CHAPTERS.md swept to zero, converted mechanically and proven by re-derivation
file construction/SHRED_PREP.md swept to zero, the same way
loom ascii_document enforce_globbed=110 enforce_derived=33 enforce_chars=0 ratchet=3225 ceiling=3232
loom control checks=63 fails=0 was=44
scope one guard widened from a directory glob to the law's own citation graph, two living pins swept, one rule page recording the answer it had named as open
status GREEN -- ascii_document witness GREEN at 143 enforced pages and zero characters, control 63 of 63, convert --verify proven on both swept pages, QA on the touched rule page B
recommend keep-going -- the sibling meters carry the same shape: rye_spoken_ascii and spoken_ascii each wall a room and name canon they do not reach
